{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/859729-hunting-tactics","id":859729,"title":"Hunting Tactics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-05T10:22:48-07:00","id":859729,"title":"Hunting Tactics","content":"So, there's this <a href=\"https://livingwithwolves.org/how-wolves-hunt/\" target=\"_blank\">nifty article</a> that talks about how wolves hunt and handle their targets. It got me wondering about what tactics people have used in their games. Not talking mechanics, more the actual strategies, the plans, the executions, the improvisations. Tell me how you have taken down prey, or how you've wanted to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T16:14:17-07:00","id":859955,"title":"","content":"Neat article.<br /> <br /> The first time we stopped a guy's car after having it drive into an alley, then approached him in various forms, so he tried to run. Before that we had shadowed him for a while to determine who he was dealing with and, then, that he'd be alone.<br /> <br /> We tend to use a lot of technology in our hunts and tracking. All of our targets, so far, have been loosely related to one another as they were all part of the same organization. So our idea of who to go after is often inspired by things we've found on a previous hunt.<br /> <br /> Usually we get all the information we can about the target first, again with a heavy leaning on technology but also following them around. We find where they live, check to see if they follow a regular routine, all aiming for a moment when we can find them alone. Mainly because once when we didn't do that before we found our target protected by two people, one of whom had some sort of magic.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of long roads through the wilderness or just empty country in our territory's state, so we've evolved the car technique. Having their car shut down, one of us goes to offer assistance in hishu while the others sneak over in urshul, then we slip in and tear the prey to shreds.<br /> <br /> So far all our prey has been humans, and really easy when it comes to the kill. Our next target is a vampire 'master,' and we're obviously going to have to adapt a lot. We're currently still in the information-gathering phase and a Siskur-Dah hasn't been called yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-05-2016, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}